{{Quote|They came the next day. Kicked out Pre-Mor, took over the hotel.|[[Maarva Carassi Andor|Maarva Andor]], to her son Cassian|<ref name="Announcement">{{Andor|Announcement}}</ref>}}
'''Hotel Rix''',<ref name="Guide">''[[Star Wars: Dawn of Rebellion: The Visual Guide]]''</ref> also known as the '''Rix Road Hotel''',<ref name="MWCA&A 231">{{InsiderCite|231|Most Wanted: Cassian Andor and Associates}}</ref> was located on the [[planet]] [[Ferrix]],<ref name="Axe" /> at [[Fountain Square]], on [[Rix Road]]. It was located across the street from a [[Unidentified chair store|store selling chairs]], and near the [[Ferrix Depot]], the [[Ferrix bell tower]] and [[Gavalox Communications]].<ref name="Rix" /> During the [[Ambush on Ferrix|mission]] to apprehend [[Cassian Jeron Andor|Cassian Andor]], [[North-1]] took cover by this building after the [[North Team]] split up and took position.<ref name="Reckoning (episode)">{{Andor|Reckoning (episode)}}</ref> When the [[Galactic Empire]] took control over the planet, they took over the [[hotel]] and made it their new headquarters.<ref name="Axe" /> [[Tenek]] worked as a [[chef]] there.<ref name="Rix" />

{{Stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
The hotel was known as the Rix Hotel during pre-production of ''[[Star Wars: Andor]]''.<ref name="Verge">{{WebCite|url=https://www.theverge.com/23445550/star-wars-andor-production-costume-design-interview|text=Andor's designers approached it like a Star Wars period drama|date=2022-11-09|author=Andrew Webster|quote=A sketch of the Rix Hotel by Luke Hull.|work=''[[Wikipedia:The Verge|The Verge]]''|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/BeOLY|aarchivedate=2022-11-27}}</ref>

